# Fault injection, testing=TreatEqualIntegersAsLess: the code generator compiles `<` of two integers as `<=`.
# So the least int32 passes `-2147483648 < at`, after which the walk has proven that `at` is greater.
# The remainder of two integers tests for a divisor of -1 only where the dividend may be the least value of its type, because the machine traps at that one division.
# With a false range it trapped even with the switch that checks proofs.
# With CheckProofsAtRunTime (which --aot-harden=proof-checks enables), the remainder checks the dividend against its proven minimum, and the process crashes with a named error.
